  "name": "RENAL FUNCTION TESTS",
  "code": "1192",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9506%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 50%;\"><col style=\"width: 50%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Urea / BUN</td>\n<td>Elevated in kidney dysfunction, dehydration, high protein intake</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Creatinine</td>\n<td>High levels indicate impaired kidney filtration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>BUN/Creatinine Ratio</td>\n<td>Helps differentiate kidney vs. non-kidney causes of elevation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Uric Acid</td>\n<td>May be high in kidney disease, gout, or certain cancers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Electrolytes (Na⁺, K⁺, Cl⁻, HCO₃⁻)</td>\n<td>Show kidney&rsquo;s ability to maintain fluid and acid-base balance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>eGFR</td>\n<td>Most reliable measure of kidney function. Lower values = reduced kidney performance</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
